rSkill physical CAP L3 acceptance","parents":["c8a6a5e09ddc54fc295d6694898f8e107d3444ae"],"sha":"29505dc66cd7e40e678f87f294145eab92f3399f"},{"author_date":"2026-09-27T12:16:51Z","committer_date":"2026-09-27T12:16:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform/commit/15bf65f8e4a37a31df2725c1226d24c0e45ff05a","message":"Test: hash BrowserSkill L3 browser identity evidence","parents":["29505dc66cd7e40e678f87f294145eab92f3399f"],"sha":"15bf65f8e4a37a31df2725c1226d24c0e45ff05a"},{"author_date":"2026-09-27T12:16:53Z","committer_date":"2026-09-27T12:16:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform/commit/35327bd6cb0346968ec6e66dfb587b2a1f2b6896","message":"Test: syntax-check BrowserSkill physical L3 harness","parents":["15bf65f8e4a37a31df2725c1226d24c0e45ff05a"],"sha":"35327bd6cb0346968ec6e66dfb587b2a1f2b6896"},{"author_date":"2026-09-27T12:17:58Z","committer_date":"2026-09-27T12:17:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform/commit/147889209da887060d18c708b59674cb37bfcee6","message":"Test: bind BrowserSkill L3 cleanup to exact created session","parents":["35327bd6cb0346968ec6e66dfb587b2a1f2b6896"],"sha":"147889209da887060d18c708b59674cb37bfcee6"},{"author_date":"2026-09-27T12:19:02Z","committer_date":"2026-09-27T12:19:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform/commit/faf9c1a3226a21b112ab388cd5b9f91c8fdc4af5","message":"Docs: pin exact BrowserSkill physical L3 harness","parents":["147889209da887060d18c708b59674cb37bfcee6"],"sha":"faf9c1a3226a21b112ab388cd5b9f91c8fdc4af5"}],"issue_comments":[],"issue_reactions":[],"pr_number":181,"pull_request":{"base":{"ref":"feature/cap-core-freeze-audit-fixes","repo":"BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform","repo_id":1326588757,"repo_node_id":"R_kgDOTxIjVQ","sha":"ca6923924952a2f457dc12e3604c97034a8fae23"},"body":"## Goal\n\nRe-enter BrowserSkill integration on the frozen CAP Core v1 head from PR #175 and prevent the old \"small first slice\" from becoming an accidental permanent capability ceiling.\n\n## Base\n\n- stacked on `feature/cap-core-freeze-audit-fixes`\n- base SHA: `ca6923924952a2f457dc12e3604c97034a8fae23`\n\n## Fresh Stage Research\n\n`project-context/BROWSERSKILL_CAP_PROVIDER_REENTRY.md` records the fresh stage-research/source-code-research result.\n\nDecision: **PROCEED** with a full capability-preserving BrowserSkill provider.\n\nPinned upstream:\n\n- Tencent/BrowserSkill `cli-v0.3.1`\n- Tencent/BrowserSkill `ext-v0.3.1`\n- both -> `da6bf4eed2dd7256567e152df8c903c87f6598c3`\n- protocol `1.3`\n\n## Invariant added first\n\nThe provider may not silently forget BrowserSkill capabilities.\n\nThis branch pins an upstream inventory fixture generated from the exact upstream source and classifies every pinned protocol method in a CAP-owned manifest.\n\nCurrent pinned inventory:\n\n- 59 protocol methods\n- all six upstream grouped model-facing browser tools\n- all grouped actions\n\nUnknown BrowserSkill version/protocol fails closed.\n\nHigh-consequence capabilities such as evaluate/debug network writes/record-audit and cross-capability upload/download stay **explicitly represented**, not silently omitted. Their CAP authority remains blocked or grant-gated until a truthful consequence contract exists.\n\n## Important architecture result\n\nThis is not a new BrowserSkill recovery framework.\n\nBrowserSkill session lifecycle/recovery remains provider-owned where upstream implements it. CAP Core remains authoritative for authorization, WorkingState, ExpectedEffect, ACK-loss/UNKNOWN reconciliation, LoopGuard and Finish Gate.\n\nProvider choice is browser-execution/session scoped, never per individual ref/action.\n\n## Current implementation status in this draft\n\nImplemented:\n\n- fresh Core-#175 re-entry;\n- exhaustive BrowserSkill 0.3.1 capability manifest;\n- exact upstream inventory fixture;\n- runtime version/protocol fail-closed helper;\n- acceptance guard for exact inventory equality and explicit high-consequence classification.\n\nNot yet complete:\n\n- BrowserSkill transport/provider binding;\n- public semantic Browser schema expansion required to use the broader BrowserSkill grouped actions;\n- provider conformance/fault tests and target-Windows physical acceptance.\n\nThis PR must remain draft until the full provider contract described by the research brief is implemented and reviewed.\n","closed_at":null,"created_at":"2026-09-27T09:48:15Z","draft":true,"head":{"ref":"feature/browserskill-provider-full-contract","repo":"BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform","repo_id":1326588757,"repo_node_id":"R_kgDOTxIjVQ","sha":"faf9c1a3226a21b112ab388cd5b9f91c8fdc4af5"},"html_url":"https://github.com/BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform/pull/181","id":4653064300,"locked":false,"merge_commit_sha":null,"merged_at":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTxIjVc8AAAABFVggbA","number":181,"state":"open","title":"Browser: integrate full BrowserSkill provider contract on Core v1","updated_at":"2026-09-27T12:19:03Z","user":{"id":225327645,"login":"BogdanAIP","type":"User"}},"repository":"BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform","repository_id":1326588757,"repository_node_id":"R_kgDOTxIjVQ","review_comments":[],"reviews":[],"schema_version":"github_pr_evidence_snapshot_v1","source":{"api_base":"https://api.github.com","pull_request_url":"https://github.com/BogdanAIP/chat-agent-platform/pull/181"}}
